Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:04.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the archives of St\NAndrews University
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.31,0:00:07.63,Cap,,0,0,0,,in Scotland, an\Nancient leather
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.65,0:00:12.48,Cap,,0,0,0,,tome from 1578 holds a\Ndrawing of a towering,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.50,0:00:16.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,skeletal man with\Nbulging forehead
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.16,0:00:19.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,veins and sunken dark\Neyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.37,0:00:22.76,Cap,,0,0,0,,His name was Herbert\NSolomon, and the town
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.78,0:00:26.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,that feared him made a\Nfatal mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.24,0:00:29.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,In the winter of 1577,\Nchildren
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.16,0:00:32.25,Cap,,0,0,0,,began vanishing from\Nthe isolated
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.27,0:00:34.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,village of Ettrick.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.36,0:00:37.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,First little Alana by\Nan old stone well,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.59,0:00:40.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,then nine more\Nchildren torn from
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.24,0:00:43.18,Cap,,0,0,0,,the freezing\Ncobblestone streets.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.20,0:00:46.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,Terrified parents\Nturned their suspicion
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.70,0:00:49.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,toward an outsider\Nliving deep
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.32,0:00:52.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,in the woods: Herbert\NSolomon.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.39,0:00:55.11,Cap,,0,0,0,,Ravaged by an\Nemaciated wasting
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.13,0:00:57.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,sickness, Solomon\Nlived
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.15,0:00:59.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,in a secluded cabin,\Ncarving
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.62,0:01:01.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,beautiful wooden dolls\Nand
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.92,0:01:04.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,leaving them on tree\Nstumps
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.30,0:01:06.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,for the local\Nchildren.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.63,0:01:09.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,But fear blinded the\Ntownsfolk.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.17,0:01:12.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,A mob marched into the\Npines, barred
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.18,0:01:15.29,Cap,,0,0,0,,his cabin, and burned\Nhim alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.31,0:01:18.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,Yet the disappearances\Ndid not stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.37,0:01:22.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,A dense fog swallowed\NEttrick, and Solomon's
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.33,0:01:24.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,tall, shadowy phantom\Nbegan
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.76,0:01:28.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,stalking the\Ncourtyards at night.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.04,0:01:31.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,Snatched from her bed,\Nanother girl vanished.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.46,0:01:34.55,Cap,,0,0,0,,Even inside the stone\Nchurch, his tall
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.57,0:01:37.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,form flickered behind\Nthe pillars.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.80,0:01:41.03,Cap,,0,0,0,,Desperate, the local\Nvicar and armed
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.05,0:01:44.37,Cap,,0,0,0,,men ambushed the\Nfigure in the street
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.39,0:01:47.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,with torches and holy\Nwater.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.22,0:01:50.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,Trapped and burning,\Nthe gaunt spirit
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.22,0:01:52.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,darted into an open\Ncottage.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.79,0:01:56.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,The mob pursued him\Ninside, discovering
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.17,0:01:59.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,a trembling child who\Nwhispered: Below.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.00,0:02:02.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,Descending into the\Ndark cellar vault,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.77,0:02:04.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,they uncovered the\Ntruth.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.88,0:02:07.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,Chained to the damp\Nstone walls were
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.76,0:02:10.51,Cap,,0,0,0,,all the missing\Nchildren—alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.53,0:02:13.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,And dead upon the\Nfloor lay Tom
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.17,0:02:15.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,Sutherland, the father\Nof
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.30,0:02:18.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,the very first missing\Ngirl.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.14,0:02:21.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,Consumed by drunken\Nmadness, Sutherland
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.36,0:02:24.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,had taken the children\Nhimself.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.22,0:02:27.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,He was about to murder\Nanother captive
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.21,0:02:29.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,when Herbert Solomon\Nburst
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.26,0:02:32.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,into the cellar,\Nbreaking the killer's
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.26,0:02:34.59,Cap,,0,0,0,,neck to save the\Ninnocent.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.61,0:02:36.69,Cap,,0,0,0,,The man they burned\Nwas their
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.71,0:02:38.59,Cap,,0,0,0,,protector all along.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.61,0:02:41.89,Cap,,0,0,0,,Centuries later, near\Nthe same woods,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.91,0:02:45.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,a little girl slipped\Ninto a raging
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.03,0:02:48.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,river, swept toward\Njagged rocks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.26,0:02:51.33,Cap,,0,0,0,,From the forest bank,\Na tall, gaunt
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.35,0:02:53.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,figure burst forth,\Nplunging a
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.99,0:02:57.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,pale, skeletal arm\Ninto the churning
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.16,0:03:00.05,Cap,,0,0,0,,water to pull her to\Nsafety.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.07,0:03:03.23,Cap,,0,0,0,,Even in death, Herbert\NSolomon was
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.25,0:03:06.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,the kindest and\Ngentlest of souls.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.88,0:03:09.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,Would you have judged\Nhim by his face?
